    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.notify\n\n### Description\n\nHi, It would be nice if you allow the users to pass the border they want for `nvim.notify` window - e.g. one of default ones like \r\n`none`, `single`, `double`, `rounded`, `solid`, `shadow`. Right now `single` is hardcocded. I noticed `none` works too, but `solid` is not working - which my personal preference.\r\nThanks for your time and consideration.",
